{"name":"Conclave","hex":"#abb9d7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"conclave","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The set of apartments in which cardinals are secluded while the process to elect a pope takes place.\n\nA group of cardinals assembled to elect a new pope.\n\n The cardinals of the Roman Catholic Church collectively.\n\nA closed assembly at which cardinals elect a pope.","The set of apartments in which cardinals are secluded while the process to elect a pope takes place."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To participate in a closed, private, or secret meeting.","Of a cardinal: to attend a closed assembly to elect a pope."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conclave"}],"entries":[{"title":"Conclave","blocks":[{"text":"A conclave is a gathering of the College of Cardinals convened to appoint the pope of the Catholic Church. Catholics consider the pope to be the apostolic successor of Saint Peter and the earthly head of the Catholic Church."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Cappella_Sistina_-_2005.jpg/330px-Cappella_Sistina_-_2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conclave"},{"title":"Conclave (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Conclave is a 2024 political thriller film directed by Edward Berger and written by Peter Straughan, based on the 2016 novel by Robert Harris. The film stars Ralph Fiennes, Stanley Tucci, John Lithgow, Sergio Castellitto, and Isabella Rossellini. In the film, Cardinal Thomas Lawrence (Fiennes) organizes a conclave to elect the next pope and finds himself investigating secrets and scandals about the major candidates."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/76/Conclave_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conclave_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Domus_Sanctae_Marthae_from_the_Dome_of_St._Peter%27s.jpg/500px-Domus_Sanctae_Marthae_from_the_Dome_of_St._Peter%27s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Domus_Sanctae_Marthae_from_the_Dome_of_St._Peter%27s.jpg/1280px-Domus_Sanctae_Marthae_from_the_Dome_of_St._Peter%27s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Domus_Sanctae_Marthae_from_the_Dome_of_St._Peter%27s.jpg/500px-Domus_Sanctae_Marthae_from_the_Dome_of_St._Peter%27s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Since the 2005 papal conclave, the cardinal electors reside in the Domus Sanctae Marthae for the length of the conclave.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADomus_Sanctae_Marthae_from_the_Dome_of_St._Peter's.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Cardinal_Camerlengo_certifying_a_papal_death.JPG/330px-Cardinal_Camerlengo_certifying_a_papal_death.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Cardinal_Camerlengo_certifying_a_papal_death.JPG/330px-Cardinal_Camerlengo_certifying_a_papal_death.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The camerlengo proclaiming a papal death","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACardinal_Camerlengo_certifying_a_papal_death.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/John_Paul_II_funeral_long_shot.jpg/500px-John_Paul_II_funeral_long_shot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/John_Paul_II_funeral_long_shot.jpg/500px-John_Paul_II_funeral_long_shot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cardinals, bishops and priests attending the funeral of Pope John Paul II","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJohn_Paul_II_funeral_long_shot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Folded_conclave_ballot.jpg/330px-Folded_conclave_ballot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Folded_conclave_ballot.jpg/330px-Folded_conclave_ballot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cardinals formerly used these intricate ballot papers, one of which is shown folded above. The text Latin reads \"Name\" and \"Signature\" at bottom, with the middle text translating to, \"I choose as Supreme Pontiff my most reverend lord, the Lord Cardinal [name].\" Currently, the ballots are simple cards, folded once, like a note card, with the words \"I elect as Supreme Pontiff\" printed in Latin on them.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFolded_conclave_ballot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Card._Mahony%27s_Scrutiny_Ballot%2C_2013.jpg/500px-Card._Mahony%27s_Scrutiny_Ballot%2C_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Card._Mahony%27s_Scrutiny_Ballot%2C_2013.jpg/1280px-Card._Mahony%27s_Scrutiny_Ballot%2C_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Card._Mahony%27s_Scrutiny_Ballot%2C_2013.jpg/500px-Card._Mahony%27s_Scrutiny_Ballot%2C_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Today, cardinal electors receive copies of multiple ballot cards, scrutiny ballots, and a copy of Ordo Rituum Conclavis (Order of Conclave Rites). Shown above are the ballot papers of Cardinal Roger Mahony used in the 2013 conclave.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACard._Mahony's_Scrutiny_Ballot%2C_2013.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Conclave_1903_scrutin.jpg/500px-Conclave_1903_scrutin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Conclave_1903_scrutin.jpg/500px-Conclave_1903_scrutin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Scrutiny during the conclave of 1903","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AConclave_1903_scrutin.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Konklave_%E2%80%93_p%C3%A1len%C3%AD_hlasovac%C3%ADch_l%C3%ADstk%C5%AF_%28Pestr%C3%BD_t%C3%BDden%2C_4._3._1939%29.jpg/500px-Konklave_%E2%80%93_p%C3%A1len%C3%AD_hlasovac%C3%ADch_l%C3%ADstk%C5%AF_%28Pestr%C3%BD_t%C3%BDden%2C_4._3._1939%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Konklave_%E2%80%93_p%C3%A1len%C3%AD_hlasovac%C3%ADch_l%C3%ADstk%C5%AF_%28Pestr%C3%BD_t%C3%BDden%2C_4._3._1939%29.jpg/500px-Konklave_%E2%80%93_p%C3%A1len%C3%AD_hlasovac%C3%ADch_l%C3%ADstk%C5%AF_%28Pestr%C3%BD_t%C3%BDden%2C_4._3._1939%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration of the burning of ballots (1939)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKonklave_%E2%80%93_p%C3%A1len%C3%AD_hlasovac%C3%ADch_l%C3%ADstk%C5%AF_(Pestr%C3%BD_t%C3%BDden%2C_4._3._1939).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Fumo_negro.jpg/330px-Fumo_negro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Fumo_negro.jpg/330px-Fumo_negro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Black smoke in the Sistine Chapel, indicating there has been no two